Source: globalprotect-openconnect-tray
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: afonsusousa <afonso.rocha@outlook.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
  autoconf,
  automake,
  autopoint,
  libtool,
  patch,
  pkg-config,
  make (>= 4),
  gettext,
  file,
  perl,
  libssl-dev,
  libxml2-dev,
  zlib1g-dev,
  liblz4-dev,
  libgnutls28-dev,
  libp11-kit-dev,
  nettle-dev,
  libgmp-dev,
  libgtk-3-dev,
  libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev,
  libsoup-3.0-dev,
  libdbus-1-dev,
  librsvg2-dev,
  desktop-file-utils,
  xz-utils,
  nodejs (>= 20.19),
  npm,
  cargo-@RUST_VERSION@,
  rustc-@RUST_VERSION@
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/afonsusousa/GlobalProtect-openconnect

Package: globalprotect-openconnect-tray
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  pkexec | policykit-1,
  xdg-utils,
  libayatana-appindicator3-1
Conflicts: globalprotect-openconnect
Replaces: globalprotect-openconnect
Provides: globalprotect-openconnect-cli (= @GP_VERSION@)
Description: GlobalProtect VPN client with a tray GUI (VIBE CODED, use at your own risk)
 *** WARNING: THIS IS VIBE CODED ***
 The tray app was written almost entirely by an AI coding assistant (Claude)
 with minimal human review. It handles VPN sign-in credentials and drives a
 privileged (root) service. It has not been audited. Use it at your own risk;
 there is no warranty of any kind.
 .
 The open-source components of GlobalProtect-openconnect @GP_VERSION@
 (gpclient, gpservice, gpauth), built from source without the proprietary GUI,
 plus a free tray icon and compact connection window that drives them.
